 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2017-05-25",
   "text": "Fairness for Struggling Students Act of 2017\n This bill amends federal bankruptcy law to make privately issued student loans dischargeable in bankruptcy. Under current law, student loans (whether issued privately or by a governmental unit) are dischargeable only if excepting the loans from dischargeability would impose undue hardship on the debtor and the debtor's dependents."
  }
